IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa13-ch5-payment.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 17 Chapter 5 (ss 580 to 592): payment for shares.
-- Lines 7895-8008 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively, written from the text alone.
-- How to read an answer: see the header of coa13-ch1-shares.l4. A liability to pay "an amount ... with interest at the appropriate
-- rate" answers its principal as a NUMBER; the period for which interest runs is not stated by the text, so interest is not computed
-- (fork F-interest in NOTES.md); the rate is s 592(1). Every name begins with the section label it implements.

§ `Part 17, Chapter 5: Payment for shares`

§§ `General rules (ss 580 to 583)`

-- ---- s 580: Shares not to be allotted at a discount ------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7898 | (1) A company's shares must not be allotted at a discount.
@ref s 580(1) a company's shares must not be allotted at a discount (src:7898)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the consideration received for the shares, including any premium` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 580(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited because it is at a discount` MEANS
    IF `the value of the consideration received for the shares, including any premium` LESS THAN `the nominal value of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company's shares must not be allotted at a discount" says nothing of an allotment that is not at a discount

-- src:7899 | (2) If shares are allotted in contravention of this section, the allottee is liable to pay the company an amount equal to the amount of the discount, with interest at the appropriate rate.
@ref s 580(2) the allottee is liable to pay the company an amount equal to the discount, with interest at the appropriate rate (src:7899)
GIVEN `the shares are allotted in contravention of section 580` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 580(2) the allottee is liable to pay the company the amount of the discount` MEANS
    IF `the shares are allotted in contravention of section 580`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares are allotted in contravention of this section, the allottee is liable" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

@ref s 580(2) the amount of the discount (src:7899)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the consideration received for the shares, including any premium` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 580(2) the amount of the discount` MEANS
    max 0 (`the nominal value of the shares` MINUS `the value of the consideration received for the shares, including any premium`)

-- ---- s 581: Provision for different amounts to be paid on shares -----------------------------------------

-- src:7901 | A company, if so authorised by its articles, may—
-- src:7902 | (a) make arrangements on the issue of shares for a difference between the shareholders in the amounts and times of payment of calls on their shares;
@ref s 581(a) a company authorised by its articles may make arrangements for different amounts and times of payment of calls (src:7901-7902)
GIVEN `the company is authorised by its articles to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements are made on the issue of shares for a difference between the shareholders in the amounts and times of payment of calls on their shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(a) the company may make the arrangements` MEANS
    IF `the company is authorised by its articles to do so`
    THEN IF `the arrangements are made on the issue of shares for a difference between the shareholders in the amounts and times of payment of calls on their shares`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "make arrangements on the issue of shares for a difference between the shareholders in the amounts and times of payment of calls"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company, if so authorised by its articles, may" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)

-- src:7903 | (b) accept from any member the whole or part of the amount remaining unpaid on any shares held by him, although no part of that amount has been called up;
@ref s 581(b) a company authorised by its articles may accept the unpaid amount although none has been called up (src:7903)
GIVEN `the company is authorised by its articles to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company accepts from a member the whole or part of the amount remaining unpaid on shares held by him, although no part of that amount has been called up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(b) the company may accept the amount remaining unpaid` MEANS
    IF `the company is authorised by its articles to do so`
    THEN IF `the company accepts from a member the whole or part of the amount remaining unpaid on shares held by him, although no part of that amount has been called up`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "accept from any member the whole or part of the amount remaining unpaid on any shares held by him, although no part of that amount has been called up"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company, if so authorised by its articles, may" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)

-- src:7904 | (c) pay a dividend in proportion to the amount paid up on each share where a larger amount is paid up on some shares than on others.
@ref s 581(c) a company authorised by its articles may pay a dividend in proportion to the amount paid up where a larger amount is paid up on some shares (src:7904)
GIVEN `the company is authorised by its articles to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a larger amount is paid up on some shares than on others` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 581(c) the company may pay a dividend in proportion to the amount paid up on each share` MEANS
    IF `the company is authorised by its articles to do so`
    THEN IF `a larger amount is paid up on some shares than on others`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "pay a dividend in proportion to the amount paid up on each share where a larger amount is paid up on some shares than on others" (a "where" that fails)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company, if so authorised by its articles, may" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)

-- ---- s 582: General rule as to means of payment ----------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7906 | (1) Shares allotted by a company, and any premium on them, may be paid up in money or money's worth (including goodwill and know-how).
@ref s 582(1) shares and any premium may be paid up in money or money's worth (src:7906)
GIVEN `the payment is in money or money's worth (including goodwill and know-how)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 582(1) the shares and any premium may be paid up in this way` MEANS
    IF `the payment is in money or money's worth (including goodwill and know-how)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be paid up in money or money's worth (including goodwill and know-how)" and the section is subject to the additional rules for public companies (subsection (3))

-- src:7907 | (2) This section does not prevent a company—
-- src:7908 | (a) from allotting bonus shares to its members, or
-- src:7909 | (b) from paying up, with sums available for the purpose, any amounts for the time being unpaid on any of its shares (whether on account of the nominal value of the shares or by way of premium).
@ref s 582(2) this section does not prevent bonus shares or paying up unpaid amounts out of sums available for the purpose (src:7907-7909)
GIVEN `the company allots bonus shares to its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company pays up, with sums available for the purpose, amounts for the time being unpaid on any of its shares (whether on account of nominal value or by way of premium)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 582(2) section 582 prevents the company from doing this` MEANS
    IF `the company allots bonus shares to its members` OR `the company pays up, with sums available for the purpose, amounts for the time being unpaid on any of its shares (whether on account of nominal value or by way of premium)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not prevent a company (a) from allotting bonus shares to its members, or (b) from paying up, with sums available for the purpose, any amounts for the time being unpaid"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names two things the section does not prevent

-- src:7910 | (3) This section has effect subject to the following provisions of this Chapter (additional rules for public companies).
@ref s 582(3) this section has effect subject to the additional rules for public companies in this Chapter (src:7910)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 582(3) section 582 has effect subject to the additional rules for public companies` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(additional rules for public companies)": the additional rules are stated for public companies

-- ---- s 583: Meaning of payment in cash -------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7914 | (3) A “cash consideration” means—
-- src:7915 | (a) cash received by the company,
-- src:7916 | (b) a cheque received by the company in good faith that the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid,
-- src:7917 | (c) a release of a liability of the company for a liquidated sum,
-- src:7918 | (d) an undertaking to pay cash to the company at a future date, or
-- src:7919 | (e) payment by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement (of the company or a person acting on the company's behalf) to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash.
@ref s 583(3) "cash consideration" (src:7914-7919)
GIVEN `cash is received by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a cheque is received by the company in good faith that the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a liability of the company for a liquidated sum is released` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an undertaking to pay cash to the company at a future date is given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment is by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement (of the company or a person acting on the company's behalf) to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the means of payment is specified in an order under subsection (4) as falling within paragraph (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 583(3) the consideration is a cash consideration` MEANS
    IF     `cash is received by the company`
        OR `a cheque is received by the company in good faith that the directors have no reason for suspecting will not be paid`
        OR `a liability of the company for a liquidated sum is released`
        OR `an undertaking to pay cash to the company at a future date is given`
        OR `payment is by any other means giving rise to a present or future entitlement (of the company or a person acting on the company's behalf) to a payment, or credit equivalent to payment, in cash`
        OR `the means of payment is specified in an order under subsection (4) as falling within paragraph (e)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A “cash consideration” means— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ... or (e) ..."

-- src:7913 | (2) A share in a company is deemed paid up (as to its nominal value or any premium on it) in cash, or allotted for cash, if the consideration received for the allotment or payment up is a cash consideration.
@ref s 583(2) a share is deemed paid up in cash, or allotted for cash, if the consideration is a cash consideration (src:7913)
GIVEN `s 583(3) the consideration is a cash consideration` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 583(2) the share is deemed paid up in cash, or allotted for cash` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 583(3) the consideration is a cash consideration`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "deemed paid up ... in cash, or allotted for cash, if the consideration received for the allotment or payment up is a cash consideration" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the consideration is a cash consideration is not known

-- src:7921 | (5) In relation to the allotment or payment up of shares in a company—
-- src:7922 | (a) the payment of cash to a person other than the company, or
-- src:7923 | (b) an undertaking to pay cash to a person other than the company,
-- src:7924 | counts as consideration other than cash.
-- src:7925 | This does not apply for the purposes of Chapter 3 (allotment of equity securities: existing shareholders' right of pre-emption).
@ref s 583(5) payment of cash, or an undertaking to pay cash, to a person other than the company counts as consideration other than cash, except for Chapter 3 (src:7921-7925)
GIVEN `it is the payment of cash to a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an undertaking to pay cash to a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purposes are those of Chapter 3 (allotment of equity securities: existing shareholders' right of pre-emption)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 583(5) the payment or undertaking counts as consideration other than cash` MEANS
    IF `the purposes are those of Chapter 3 (allotment of equity securities: existing shareholders' right of pre-emption)`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply for the purposes of Chapter 3"
    ELSE IF `it is the payment of cash to a person other than the company` OR `it is an undertaking to pay cash to a person other than the company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) the payment of cash to a person other than the company, or (b) an undertaking to pay cash to a person other than the company"

-- src:7926 | (6) For the purpose of determining whether a share is or is to be allotted for cash, or paid up in cash, “cash” includes foreign currency.
@ref s 583(6) "cash" includes foreign currency (src:7926)
GIVEN `the money is foreign currency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 583(6) the money is cash for the purpose of determining whether a share is allotted for cash or paid up in cash` MEANS
    IF `the money is foreign currency`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“cash” includes foreign currency" lists one inclusion and leaves "cash" otherwise undefined

§§ `Additional rules for public companies (ss 584 to 587)`

-- ---- s 584: Public companies: shares taken by subscribers of memorandum ---------------------------------

-- src:7930 | Shares taken by a subscriber to the memorandum of a public company in pursuance of an undertaking of his in the memorandum, and any premium on the shares, must be paid up in cash.
@ref s 584 shares taken by a subscriber to the memorandum of a public company, and any premium, must be paid up in cash (src:7930)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are taken by a subscriber to the memorandum in pursuance of an undertaking of his in the memorandum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 583(2) the share is deemed paid up in cash, or allotted for cash` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 584 the shares and any premium meet the requirement to be paid up in cash` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `the shares are taken by a subscriber to the memorandum in pursuance of an undertaking of his in the memorandum`
    THEN `s 583(2) the share is deemed paid up in cash, or allotted for cash` -- JUST TRUE: met; JUST FALSE: a bare "must" not done (a fork line); NOTHING passes through
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Shares taken by a subscriber to the memorandum of a public company in pursuance of an undertaking of his in the memorandum"

-- ---- s 585: Public companies: must not accept undertaking to do work or perform services ---------------

-- src:7932 | (1) A public company must not accept at any time, in payment up of its shares or any premium on them, an undertaking given by any person that he or another should do work or perform services for the company or any other person.
@ref s 585(1) a public company must not accept an undertaking to do work or perform services in payment up of its shares or any premium (src:7932)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is given by a person that he or another should do work or perform services for the company or any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company accepts it in payment up of its shares or any premium on them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 585(1) the public company is prohibited from accepting the undertaking` MEANS
    IF     `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
       AND `the undertaking is given by a person that he or another should do work or perform services for the company or any other person`
       AND `the company accepts it in payment up of its shares or any premium on them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company must not accept at any time, in payment up of its shares or any premium on them, an undertaking given by any person that he or another should do work or perform services"

-- src:7933 | (2) If a public company accepts such an undertaking in payment up of its shares or any premium on them, the holder of the shares when they or the premium are treated as paid up (in whole or in part) by the undertaking is liable—
@ref s 585(2) if a public company accepts such an undertaking, the holder of the shares is liable to pay the company (src:7933)
GIVEN `the public company accepts such an undertaking in payment up of its shares or any premium on them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 585(2) the holder of the shares is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    IF `the public company accepts such an undertaking in payment up of its shares or any premium on them`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a public company accepts such an undertaking ... the holder of the shares ... is liable" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:7934 | (a) to pay the company in respect of those shares an amount equal to their nominal value, together with the whole of any premium or, if the case so requires, such proportion of that amount as is treated as paid up by the undertaking; and
@ref s 585(2)(a) the amount: the nominal value and the whole of any premium, or the proportion treated as paid up by the undertaking (src:7934)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole of any premium on them` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that amount that is treated as paid up by the undertaking (1 if the whole)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 585(2)(a) the amount the holder is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    (`the nominal value of the shares` PLUS `the whole of any premium on them`) TIMES `the proportion of that amount that is treated as paid up by the undertaking (1 if the whole)`

-- src:7936 | (3) The reference in subsection (2) to the holder of shares includes a person who has an unconditional right—
-- src:7937 | (a) to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares, or
-- src:7938 | (b) to have an instrument of transfer of them executed in his favour.
@ref s 585(3) the holder of shares includes a person with an unconditional right to be on the register of members or to have an instrument of transfer executed (src:7936-7938)
GIVEN `the person has an unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an unconditional right to have an instrument of transfer of them executed in his favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 585(3) the person is within the reference to the holder of shares` MEANS
    IF `the person has an unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares` OR `the person has an unconditional right to have an instrument of transfer of them executed in his favour`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a person who has an unconditional right" does not close the list

-- ---- s 586: Public companies: shares must be at least one-quarter paid up -----------------------------

-- src:7941 | (2) This does not apply to shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme.
@ref s 586(2) subsection (1) does not apply to shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme (src:7941)
GIVEN `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the share is allotted in pursuance of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 586(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the share` MEANS
    IF `the share is allotted in pursuance of the scheme`
    THEN `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This does not apply to shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme"

-- src:7940 | (1) A public company must not allot a share except as paid up at least as to one-quarter of its nominal value and the whole of any premium on it.
@ref s 586(1) a public company must not allot a share except as paid up at least as to one-quarter of its nominal value and the whole of any premium (src:7940)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominal value of the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid up on the share as to its nominal value` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium on the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount paid up on the share as to the premium` IS A NUMBER
      `s 586(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the share` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 586(1) the allotment of the share is prohibited` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
    THEN IF `s 586(2) subsection (1) does not apply to the share` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply to shares allotted in pursuance of an employees' share scheme" (the exception is met)
         ELSE IF     `the amount paid up on the share as to its nominal value` AT LEAST (`the nominal value of the share` DIVIDED BY 4)
                 AND `the amount paid up on the share as to the premium` AT LEAST `the premium on the share`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not allot a share except as paid up at least as to one-quarter of its nominal value and the whole of any premium on it" (the exception is met)
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company must not allot a share"

-- src:7943 | (a) the share is to be treated as if one-quarter of its nominal value, together with the whole of any premium on it, had been received, and
@ref s 586(3)(a) the share is treated as if one-quarter of its nominal value and the whole of any premium had been received (src:7943)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium on the share` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 586(3)(a) the amount treated as having been received for the share` MEANS
    (`the nominal value of the share` DIVIDED BY 4) PLUS `the premium on the share`

-- src:7944 | (b) the allottee is liable to pay the company the minimum amount which should have been received in respect of the share under subsection (1) (less the value of any consideration actually applied in payment up, to any extent, of the share and any premium on it), with interest at the appropriate rate.
@ref s 586(3)(b) the allottee is liable to pay the minimum amount which should have been received, less the value of consideration actually applied (src:7944)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium on the share` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of any consideration actually applied in payment up, to any extent, of the share and any premium on it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 586(3)(b) the amount the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    ((`the nominal value of the share` DIVIDED BY 4) PLUS `the premium on the share`) MINUS `the value of any consideration actually applied in payment up, to any extent, of the share and any premium on it`

-- src:7945 | (4) Subsection (3) does not apply to the allotment of bonus shares, unless the allottee knew or ought to have known the shares were allotted in contravention of this section.
@ref s 586(4) subsection (3) does not apply to bonus shares, unless the allottee knew or ought to have known of the contravention (src:7945)
GIVEN `the allotment is of bonus shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the allottee knew or ought to have known the shares were allotted in contravention of section 586` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 586(4) subsection (3) does not apply to the allotment` MEANS
    IF `the allotment is of bonus shares`
    THEN IF `the allottee knew or ought to have known the shares were allotted in contravention of section 586`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the allottee knew or ought to have known the shares were allotted in contravention of this section" (the "unless" is met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (3) does not apply to the allotment of bonus shares"

-- src:7942 | (3) If a company allots a share in contravention of this section—
@ref s 586(3) if a company allots a share in contravention of the section, the allottee is liable (src:7942)
GIVEN `the company allots the share in contravention of section 586` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 586(4) subsection (3) does not apply to the allotment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 586(3) the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    IF `the company allots the share in contravention of section 586`
    THEN IF `s 586(4) subsection (3) does not apply to the allotment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (3) does not apply to the allotment of bonus shares, unless the allottee knew or ought to have known" (the exception is met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- an exception that answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING is read as not met (fork F-586(4))
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company allots a share in contravention of this section" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- ---- s 587: Public companies: payment by long-term undertaking -----------------------------------------

-- src:7947 | (1) A public company must not allot shares as fully or partly paid up (as to their nominal value or any premium on them) otherwise than in cash if the consideration for the allotment is or includes an undertaking which is to be, or may be, performed more than five years after the date of the allotment.
@ref s 587(1) a public company must not allot shares otherwise than for cash if the consideration includes an undertaking to be performed more than five years after the allotment (src:7947)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the latest date on which the undertaking forming or included in the consideration is to be, or may be, performed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 587(1) the allotment of the shares is prohibited` MEANS
    IF `s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `the shares are allotted as fully or partly paid up otherwise than in cash`
    THEN IF `the latest date on which the undertaking forming or included in the consideration is to be, or may be, performed` GREATER THAN (`add years` `the date of the allotment` 5)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the consideration for the allotment is or includes an undertaking which is to be, or may be, performed more than five years after the date of the allotment" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company must not allot shares as fully or partly paid up (as to their nominal value or any premium on them) otherwise than in cash"

-- src:7948 | (2) If a company allots shares in contravention of subsection (1), the allottee is liable to pay the company an amount equal to the aggregate of their nominal value and the whole of any premium (or, if the case so requires, so much of that aggregate as is treated as paid up by the undertaking), with interest at the appropriate rate.
@ref s 587(2) if a company allots shares in contravention of subsection (1), the allottee is liable to pay the company the nominal value and premium (src:7948)
GIVEN `the company allots the shares in contravention of section 587(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 587(2) the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    IF `the company allots the shares in contravention of section 587(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company allots shares in contravention of subsection (1), the allottee is liable" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

@ref s 587(2) the amount: the nominal value and the whole of any premium, or so much as is treated as paid up by the undertaking (src:7948)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole of any premium on them` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up by the undertaking (1 if the whole)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 587(2) the amount the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    (`the nominal value of the shares` PLUS `the whole of any premium on them`) TIMES `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up by the undertaking (1 if the whole)`

-- src:7949 | (3) Where a contract for the allotment of shares does not contravene subsection (1), any variation of the contract that has the effect that the contract would have contravened the subsection, if the terms of the contract as varied had been its original terms, is void.
-- src:7950 | This applies also to the variation by a public company of the terms of a contract entered into before the company was re-registered as a public company.
@ref s 587(3) a variation that would have made the contract contravene subsection (1) is void (src:7949-7950)
GIVEN `the contract for the allotment does not contravene subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation is by a public company of the terms of a contract entered into before the company was re-registered as a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation has the effect that the contract would have contravened subsection (1) if the terms of the contract as varied had been its original terms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 587(3) the variation is void` MEANS
    IF `the contract for the allotment does not contravene subsection (1)` OR `the variation is by a public company of the terms of a contract entered into before the company was re-registered as a public company`
    THEN IF `the variation has the effect that the contract would have contravened subsection (1) if the terms of the contract as varied had been its original terms`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any variation of the contract that has the effect that the contract would have contravened the subsection"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a contract for the allotment of shares does not contravene subsection (1)" (a "where" that fails)

-- src:7951 | (4) Where—
-- src:7952 | (a) a public company allots shares for a consideration which consists of or includes (in accordance with subsection (1)) an undertaking that is to be performed within five years of the allotment, and
-- src:7953 | (b) the undertaking is not performed within the period allowed by the contract for the allotment of the shares,
-- src:7954 | the allottee is liable to pay the company, at the end of the period so allowed, an amount equal to the aggregate of the nominal value of the shares and the whole of any premium (or, if the case so requires, so much of that aggregate as is treated as paid up by the undertaking), with interest at the appropriate rate.
@ref s 587(4) where an undertaking within five years is not performed within the period allowed, the allottee is liable to pay the company at the end of that period (src:7951-7954)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company allots shares for a consideration which consists of or includes (in accordance with subsection (1)) an undertaking that is to be performed within five years of the allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the undertaking is not performed within the period allowed by the contract for the allotment of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 587(4) the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    IF     `s 4(2) the company is a public company`
       AND `the company allots shares for a consideration which consists of or includes (in accordance with subsection (1)) an undertaking that is to be performed within five years of the allotment`
       AND `the undertaking is not performed within the period allowed by the contract for the allotment of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where (a) a public company allots shares for a consideration which consists of or includes ... an undertaking ... within five years of the allotment, and (b) the undertaking is not performed within the period allowed" (a "where" that fails)

@ref s 587(4) the liability arises at the end of the period allowed by the contract (src:7954)
GIVEN `the end of the period allowed by the contract for the allotment of the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 587(4) the date on which the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    `the end of the period allowed by the contract for the allotment of the shares`

@ref s 587(4) the amount: the nominal value and the whole of any premium, or so much as is treated as paid up by the undertaking (src:7954)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole of any premium on them` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up by the undertaking (1 if the whole)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 587(4) the amount the allottee is liable to pay the company` MEANS
    (`the nominal value of the shares` PLUS `the whole of any premium on them`) TIMES `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up by the undertaking (1 if the whole)`

-- src:7955 | (5) References in this section to a contract for the allotment of shares include an ancillary contract relating to payment in respect of them.
@ref s 587(5) a contract for the allotment of shares includes an ancillary contract relating to payment (src:7955)
GIVEN `it is an ancillary contract relating to payment in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 587(5) the contract is treated as a contract for the allotment of shares` MEANS
    IF `it is an ancillary contract relating to payment in respect of the shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include an ancillary contract relating to payment in respect of them" does not close the list

§§ `Supplementary provisions (ss 588 to 592)`

-- ---- s 588: Liability of subsequent holders of shares ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:7962 | (2) A person otherwise liable under subsection (1) is exempted from that liability if either—
-- src:7963 | (a) he is a purchaser for value and, at the time of the purchase, he did not have actual notice of the contravention concerned, or
-- src:7964 | (b) he derived title to the shares (directly or indirectly) from a person who became a holder of them after the contravention and was not liable under subsection (1).
@ref s 588(2) a person otherwise liable is exempted if a purchaser for value without actual notice, or if he derived title from a person not liable (src:7962-7964)
GIVEN `he is a purchaser for value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time of the purchase he did not have actual notice of the contravention concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he derived title to the shares (directly or indirectly) from a person who became a holder of them after the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person was not liable under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 588(2) the person is exempted from the liability` MEANS
    IF     (`he is a purchaser for value` AND `at the time of the purchase he did not have actual notice of the contravention concerned`)
        OR (`he derived title to the shares (directly or indirectly) from a person who became a holder of them after the contravention` AND `that person was not liable under subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is exempted from that liability if either (a) ... or (b) ..." (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:7958 | (1) If a person becomes a holder of shares in respect of which—
-- src:7959 | (a) there has been a contravention of any provision of this Chapter, and
-- src:7960 | (b) by virtue of that contravention another is liable to pay any amount under the provision contravened,
-- src:7961 | that person is also liable to pay that amount (jointly and severally with any other person so liable), subject as follows.
@ref s 588(1) a person who becomes a holder of shares in respect of which another is liable is also liable, subject to subsection (2) (src:7958-7961)
GIVEN `there has been a contravention of a provision of Chapter 5 in respect of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by virtue of that contravention another is liable to pay an amount under the provision contravened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 588(2) the person is exempted from the liability` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 588(1) the person who becomes a holder is also liable to pay the amount` MEANS
    IF `there has been a contravention of a provision of Chapter 5 in respect of the shares` AND `by virtue of that contravention another is liable to pay an amount under the provision contravened`
    THEN IF `s 588(2) the person is exempted from the liability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person otherwise liable under subsection (1) is exempted from that liability if either" (the exemption is met)
         ELSE JUST TRUE -- an exemption that answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING is read as not met (fork F-588)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person becomes a holder of shares in respect of which (a) there has been a contravention ... and (b) by virtue of that contravention another is liable" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:7965 | (3) References in this section to a holder, in relation to shares in a company, include any person who has an unconditional right—
-- src:7966 | (a) to be included in the company's register of members ... in respect of those shares, or
-- src:7967 | (b) to have an instrument of transfer of the shares executed in his favour.
@ref s 588(3) the holder includes a person with an unconditional right to be on the register of members or to have an instrument of transfer executed (src:7965-7967)
GIVEN `the person has an unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an unconditional right to have an instrument of transfer of the shares executed in his favour` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 588(3) the person is within the reference to a holder of shares` MEANS
    IF `the person has an unconditional right to be included in the company's register of members in respect of those shares` OR `the person has an unconditional right to have an instrument of transfer of the shares executed in his favour`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include any person who has an unconditional right" does not close the list

-- src:7968 | (4) This section applies in relation to a failure to carry out a term of a contract as mentioned in section 587(4) (public companies: payment by long-term undertaking) as it applies in relation to a contravention of a provision of this Chapter.
@ref s 588(4) the section applies to a failure to carry out a term of a contract as mentioned in s 587(4) (src:7968)
GIVEN `the failure is to carry out a term of a contract as mentioned in section 587(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 588(4) section 588 applies to the failure as it applies to a contravention` MEANS
    IF `the failure is to carry out a term of a contract as mentioned in section 587(4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies in relation to a failure to carry out a term of a contract as mentioned in section 587(4)"

-- ---- s 589: Power of court to grant relief ---------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:7970 | (1) This section applies in relation to liability under—
-- src:7971 | section 585(2) (liability of allottee in case of breach by public company of prohibition on accepting undertaking to do work or perform services),
-- src:7972 | section 587(2) or (4) (liability of allottee in case of breach by public company of prohibition on payment by long-term undertaking), or
-- src:7973 | section 588 (liability of subsequent holders of shares),
-- src:7974 | as it applies in relation to a contravention of those sections.
@ref s 589(1) the section applies to liability under s 585(2), s 587(2) or (4), and s 588 (src:7970-7974)
GIVEN `the liability is under section 585(2), 587(2) or (4), or 588` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 589(1) section 589 applies to the liability` MEANS
    IF `the liability is under section 585(2), 587(2) or (4), or 588`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies in relation to liability under section 585(2) ..., section 587(2) or (4) ..., or section 588"

-- src:7975 | (2) A person who—
-- src:7976 | (a) is subject to any such liability to a company in relation to payment in respect of shares in the company, or
-- src:7977 | (b) is subject to any such liability to a company by virtue of an undertaking given to it in, or in connection with, payment for shares in the company,
-- src:7978 | may apply to the court to be exempted in whole or in part from the liability.
@ref s 589(2) a person subject to the liability may apply to the court to be exempted in whole or in part (src:7975-7978)
GIVEN `s 589(1) section 589 applies to the liability` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to the liability to a company in relation to payment in respect of shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to the liability to a company by virtue of an undertaking given to it in, or in connection with, payment for shares in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 589(2) the person may apply to the court to be exempted from the liability in whole or in part` MEANS
    IF     `s 589(1) section 589 applies to the liability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
       AND (    `the person is subject to the liability to a company in relation to payment in respect of shares in the company`
             OR `the person is subject to the liability to a company by virtue of an undertaking given to it in, or in connection with, payment for shares in the company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who (a) is subject to any such liability ... or (b) is subject to any such liability ... may apply to the court"

-- src:7979 | (3) In the case of a liability within subsection (2)(a), the court may exempt the applicant from the liability only if and to the extent that it appears to the court just and equitable to do so having regard to—
-- src:7980 | (a) whether the applicant has paid, or is liable to pay, any amount in respect of—
-- src:7981 | (i) any other liability arising in relation to those shares under any provision of this Chapter or Chapter 6, or
-- src:7982 | (ii) any liability arising by virtue of any undertaking given in or in connection with payment for those shares;
-- src:7983 | (b) whether any person other than the applicant has paid or is likely to pay, whether in pursuance of any order of the court or otherwise, any such amount;
-- src:7984 | (c) whether the applicant or any other person—
-- src:7985 | (i) has performed in whole or in part, or is likely so to perform any such undertaking, or
-- src:7986 | (ii) has done or is likely to do any other thing in payment or part payment for the shares.
@ref s 589(3) in the case of a liability within subsection (2)(a), the court may exempt the applicant only if and to the extent that it appears just and equitable (src:7979-7986)
GIVEN `it appears to the court just and equitable to exempt the applicant, having regard to whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of any other liability or undertaking, whether any other person has paid or is likely to pay any such amount, and whether the applicant or any other person has performed or is likely to perform any such undertaking or done any other thing in payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 589(3) the court may exempt the applicant from a liability within subsection (2)(a)` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court just and equitable to exempt the applicant, having regard to whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of any other liability or undertaking, whether any other person has paid or is likely to pay any such amount, and whether the applicant or any other person has performed or is likely to perform any such undertaking or done any other thing in payment`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may exempt the applicant from the liability only if and to the extent that it appears to the court just and equitable to do so" (the judgment of the court is a plain input)

-- src:7987 | (4) In the case of a liability within subsection (2)(b), the court may exempt the applicant from the liability only if and to the extent that it appears to the court just and equitable to do so having regard to—
-- src:7988 | (a) whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of liability arising in relation to the shares under any provision of this Chapter or Chapter 6;
-- src:7989 | (b) whether any person other than the applicant has paid or is likely to pay, whether in pursuance of any order of the court or otherwise, any such amount.
@ref s 589(4) in the case of a liability within subsection (2)(b), the court may exempt the applicant only if and to the extent that it appears just and equitable (src:7987-7989)
GIVEN `it appears to the court just and equitable to exempt the applicant, having regard to whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of liability arising in relation to the shares under Chapter 5 or Chapter 6, and whether any other person has paid or is likely to pay any such amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 589(4) the court may exempt the applicant from a liability within subsection (2)(b)` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the court just and equitable to exempt the applicant, having regard to whether the applicant has paid or is liable to pay any amount in respect of liability arising in relation to the shares under Chapter 5 or Chapter 6, and whether any other person has paid or is likely to pay any such amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the court may exempt the applicant from the liability only if and to the extent that it appears to the court just and equitable to do so" (the judgment of the court is a plain input)

-- src:7990 | (5) In determining whether it should exempt the applicant in whole or in part from any liability, the court must have regard to the following overriding principles—
-- src:7991 | (a) a company that has allotted shares should receive money or money's worth at least equal in value to the aggregate of the nominal value of those shares and the whole of any premium or, if the case so requires, so much of that aggregate as is treated as paid up;
@ref s 589(5)(a) overriding principle: the company should receive money or money's worth at least equal to the nominal value and premium (src:7990-7991)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the whole of any premium on them` IS A NUMBER
      `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up (1 if the whole)` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the money or money's worth the company would receive if the exemption were granted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 589(5)(a) the principle that the company should receive at least the aggregate is satisfied` MEANS
    IF `the value of the money or money's worth the company would receive if the exemption were granted` AT LEAST ((`the nominal value of the shares` PLUS `the whole of any premium on them`) TIMES `the proportion of that aggregate that is treated as paid up (1 if the whole)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company that has allotted shares should receive money or money's worth at least equal in value to the aggregate of the nominal value of those shares and the whole of any premium" (the principle is not satisfied)

-- src:7992 | (b) subject to that, where a company would, if the court did not grant the exemption, have more than one remedy against a particular person, it should be for the company to decide which remedy it should remain entitled to pursue.
@ref s 589(5)(b) subject to that, where the company has more than one remedy it is for the company to decide which to pursue (src:7992)
GIVEN `the company would, if the court did not grant the exemption, have more than one remedy against a particular person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 589(5)(a) the principle that the company should receive at least the aggregate is satisfied` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 589(5)(b) it is for the company to decide which remedy it should remain entitled to pursue` MEANS
    IF `the company would, if the court did not grant the exemption, have more than one remedy against a particular person`
    THEN IF `s 589(5)(a) the principle that the company should receive at least the aggregate is satisfied` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to that": the first principle prevails and the text does not say what follows when it is not satisfied
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where a company would, if the court did not grant the exemption, have more than one remedy against a particular person"

-- src:7993 | (6) If a person brings proceedings against another (“the contributor”) for a contribution in respect of liability to a company arising under any provision of this Chapter or Chapter 6 and it appears to the court that the contributor is liable to make such a contribution, the court may, if and to the extent that it appears to it just and equitable to do so having regard to the respective culpability (in respect of the liability to the company) of the contributor and the person bringing the proceedings—
-- src:7994 | (a) exempt the contributor in whole or in part from his liability to make such a contribution, or
-- src:7995 | (b) order the contributor to make a larger contribution than, but for this subsection, he would be liable to make.
@ref s 589(6) in contribution proceedings the court may exempt the contributor or order a larger contribution (src:7993-7995)
GIVEN `a person brings proceedings against another (“the contributor”) for a contribution in respect of liability to a company arising under any provision of Chapter 5 or Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court that the contributor is liable to make such a contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court just and equitable to do so, having regard to the respective culpability (in respect of the liability to the company) of the contributor and the person bringing the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 589(6) the court may exempt the contributor in whole or in part, or order a larger contribution` MEANS
    IF     `a person brings proceedings against another (“the contributor”) for a contribution in respect of liability to a company arising under any provision of Chapter 5 or Chapter 6`
       AND `it appears to the court that the contributor is liable to make such a contribution`
    THEN IF `it appears to the court just and equitable to do so, having regard to the respective culpability (in respect of the liability to the company) of the contributor and the person bringing the proceedings`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, if and to the extent that it appears to it just and equitable to do so having regard to the respective culpability" (a grant: a failed condition is not the text's no, fork F-grant-gate)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person brings proceedings against another (“the contributor”) for a contribution ... and it appears to the court that the contributor is liable to make such a contribution"

-- ---- s 590: Penalty for contravention of this Chapter ----------------------------------------------------

-- src:7997 | (1) If a company contravenes any of the provisions of this Chapter, an offence is committed by—
-- src:7998 | (a) the company, and
-- src:7999 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 590(1) offence: if a company contravenes the Chapter, the company and every officer in default (src:7997-7999)
GIVEN `the company contravenes a provision of Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 590(1)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company contravenes a provision of Chapter 5`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company contravenes any of the provisions of this Chapter, an offence is committed by (a) the company" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

@ref s 590(1)(b) offence by every officer of the company who is in default (src:7999)
GIVEN `the company contravenes a provision of Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 590(1)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `the company contravenes a provision of Chapter 5`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 1121 is not among the sources
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company contravenes any of the provisions of this Chapter, an offence is committed by ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))

-- src:8000 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:8001 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to a fine;
-- src:8002 | (b) on summary conviction, to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum.
@ref s 590(2)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment (src:8000-8002)
`s 590(2)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 590(2)(b) penalty on summary conviction (src:8002)
`s 590(2)(b) penalty on summary conviction` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 590(2) a person guilty of an offence under s 590 is liable (src:8000-8002)
GIVETH A LIST OF Penalty
`s 590(2) the penalties for an offence under section 590` MEANS
    LIST `s 590(2)(a) penalty on conviction on indictment`, `s 590(2)(b) penalty on summary conviction`

-- ---- s 591: Enforceability of undertakings to do work etc ------------------------------------------------

-- src:8004 | (1) An undertaking given by any person, in or in connection with payment for shares in a company, to do work or perform services or to do any other thing, if it is enforceable by the company apart from this Chapter, is so enforceable notwithstanding that there has been a contravention in relation to it of a provision of this Chapter or Chapter 6.
@ref s 591(1) an undertaking enforceable by the company apart from the Chapter remains enforceable despite a contravention (src:8004)
GIVEN `the undertaking is given by a person, in or in connection with payment for shares in a company, to do work or perform services or to do any other thing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is enforceable by the company apart from Chapter 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 591(1) the undertaking is enforceable by the company despite a contravention of Chapter 5 or Chapter 6` MEANS
    IF `the undertaking is given by a person, in or in connection with payment for shares in a company, to do work or perform services or to do any other thing`
    THEN IF `it is enforceable by the company apart from Chapter 5`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is enforceable by the company apart from this Chapter, is so enforceable" (an "if" that fails: marginal reading (a))
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An undertaking given by any person, in or in connection with payment for shares in a company, to do work or perform services or to do any other thing"

-- src:8005 | (2) This is without prejudice to section 589 (power of court to grant relief etc in respect of liabilities).
@ref s 591(2) this is without prejudice to s 589 (src:8005)
GIVEN `the matter is the court's power under section 589 to grant relief in respect of liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 591(2) section 591(1) prejudices the court's power under section 589` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the court's power under section 589 to grant relief in respect of liabilities`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This is without prejudice to section 589"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of section 589 only

-- ---- s 592: The appropriate rate of interest -------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:8007 | (1) For the purposes of this Chapter the “appropriate rate” of interest is 5% per annum or such other rate as may be specified by order made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 592(1) the appropriate rate of interest is 5% per annum or such other rate as may be specified by order (src:8007)
GIVEN `the other rate specified by an order made by the Secretary of State under section 592(1), as a fraction per annum, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 592(1) the appropriate rate of interest, as a fraction per annum` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the other rate specified by an order made by the Secretary of State under section 592(1), as a fraction per annum, if there is one`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN rate
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 0.05
